## Running and testing on devices

Use the scripts in `{{OUT}}/`, not hand-typed `flutter run` / `adb install` / `xcrun devicectl` commands, whenever asked to run, launch or test the app on a phone, iPhone or this Mac:

```bash
{{OUT}}/run_all.sh        # debug build: build + install + launch on every connected Android phone, iPhone and this Mac
{{OUT}}/build_release.sh  # release build: same devices; runs standalone, so USB can be unplugged afterwards
```

- Device discovery is automatic (`adb devices`, `xcrun devicectl`, and this Mac). Ids are in `{{OUT}}/lib.sh`: Android `{{ANDROID_APP_ID}}`, iOS `{{IOS_BUNDLE_ID}}`, macOS `{{MACOS_APP_NAME}}`.
- iOS debug runs keep `flutter run` alive in the background (pid and log in `{{OUT}}/.run/`). A debug build cannot be launched on a physical iPhone with `devicectl` alone. Stop it with `kill $(cat {{OUT}}/.run/<udid>.pid)`.
- macOS is launched with `open`, never `flutter run`, so camera and mic permissions are checked against the app and not the terminal.
- Read `{{OUT}}/lib.sh` for the build/install/launch helpers before adding a new device script.
